## Summary

Phase 0 (Week 5 carry-over) is functionally closed. The perception and
control pipeline was rebuilt after the Week 6 stage migration broke the
robot's drive graph, and a straight-row closed-loop baseline was logged
with real success-rate and path-deviation numbers. An end-of-row stop
behaviour has been implemented on top of the controller as the first step
toward headland turning (deferred to a later week).

---

## What was completed

### 1. Perception pipeline (rebuilt + calibrated)
- Temporal-tracking `perception_bridge_node.py` running in `balance` mode
  (corridor-centering via left/right green-mask balance).
- Added a `balance_bias` parameter to correct camera-mount asymmetry so a
  centered robot reads offset ≈ 0. Calibrated at the field's true aisle
  centre (x = 0).
- Camera publishing confirmed at ~17 Hz on `/robot/camera/image_raw`.

### 2. Drive graph (rebuilt from scratch)
The Week 6 stage migration left the robot's Action Graph broken. It was
rebuilt in full — camera, odometry, and differential drive chains. Root
causes found and fixed (documented for future reference):
- The render product was pointed at the LiDAR prim (`XT_32_10hz`) instead
  of the RGB camera, producing black frames — repointed to the camera.
- The scene had no light; a Distant Light was added.
- Differential Controller received `dt = 0` (delta-time input unwired) and
  had its linear-velocity input wired from the Break-3-Vector Z component
  instead of X — both corrected.
- Odometry and camera chains re-verified: `/odom` ~38 Hz, camera ~17 Hz.

### 3. Straight-row closed-loop baseline (logged)
Closed-loop run on the straight-row field, robot starting at the middle
aisle (x = 0), 10 m run:

| Metric | Result |
|---|---|
| Result | **SUCCESS** (completed 10 m run) |
| Max path deviation | 0.284 m |
| Mean path deviation | 0.092 m |
| Fail threshold | 0.6 m (never approached) |

Controller: PD, kp = 0.004, kd = 0.001, linear speed 0.4 m/s.
Logged via `test_logger_node.py` → `analyze_results.py`.

### 4. End-of-row stop (implemented, testing in progress)
Added a latched end-of-row stop to `row_follower_controller.py`:
distinguishes a brief mid-aisle detection loss (hold, resume) from a
sustained loss (row has ended → latch and stop). This is the trigger point
the future headland-turn behaviour will fire from. Threshold tuning against
the field's sparse patches is in progress.

